{"event_type":"review","id":"31a12d07d6e191911479a1df4ee684af78df70cc964d14b9e7d54ce9fffe3c7a","occurred_at":"2026-11-05T10:31:57Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/ec42495edf3775e2448cb09c59a93e18b39046fa57c5397cf97baa2990222fb7","sha256":"ec42495edf3775e2448cb09c59a93e18b39046fa57c5397cf97baa2990222fb7"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/7bc53eaa8ed33af34b58ae2fd236b19ac7ff473aea13bfc98fc04385ffa1986c","sha256":"7bc53eaa8ed33af34b58ae2fd236b19ac7ff473aea13bfc98fc04385ffa1986c"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/9c3ba328cab950a1f138b96cffec893395923949ef7466f923786e054f621635","sha256":"9c3ba328cab950a1f138b96cffec893395923949ef7466f923786e054f621635"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/5e1048d972c9522aa767092cf35dc3d65c7e0a8b943622979b1be1ccd49d87c4","sha256":"5e1048d972c9522aa767092cf35dc3d65c7e0a8b943622979b1be1ccd49d87c4"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/8496babee6f587e4502f7b2e9deaba26d2c0806c3dfb41a4c604c31a732d7b27","sha256":"8496babee6f587e4502f7b2e9deaba26d2c0806c3dfb41a4c604c31a732d7b27"}],"attempt_id":"8af537efc33d547bd72d8556ecac2bedad79bbe6dc473a4bf0abe243c647a205:0:1","base":"ac634e49ca2c4b0f550d9ef77a35e50ec3ec2658","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"2ac6ce40ff008f3269fdc03fe7bd0256cea418d5","body":"**Fix the §3.3 timeout analysis. It contradicts the new batch-policy premise.**\n\nLines 453-457 now say that S3 (`merge-queue-gate.yml`) is the only promoter and that S7 is report-only. Two statements in the same section still assume that the successor gate promotes:\n\n- Lines 451-452: \"So the successor can promote a tip whose macOS leg ran longer than 20 minutes.\"\n- Lines 457-459: a slow macOS leg costs \"latency and refusal noise … not promotion.\"\n\nUnder the new premise, a timed-out S3 attempt leaves the reviewed sha unpromoted. A slow macOS leg therefore does block promotion until a re-dispatch or a fresh review status arrives.\n\nThe recommendation at lines 466-473 relies on the same stale premise. It says \"The successor's fresh-deadline attempts already tolerate a slow run.\" It also says \"both promoters are live.\" A reader could use this section to decide against raising `{{GATE_TIMEOUT_MIN}}`, and that decision would rest on a promoter that no longer promotes.\n\nEither scope the successor-promotes statements to the pre-batch design, or rewrite them for S3-only promotion. If you rewrite them, also re-derive whether the 20-minute wait should be raised.","id":"d343f92c14f3103cf2d765f629906ab28631b2e8bfa543ebba20b9ae547d795e","intervals":[],"path":"docs/w4-obligation-matrix.md","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Fix the §3.3 timeout analysis. It contradicts the new batch-policy premise."}],"head":"908cbbc900e06422bfbbab4b3a40c9eeced911bc","head_tree":"caf2bd1c0f6a76b490442f34307539ee3268e814","input_scope":[{"blob":"fb4ded897a827b876263897d1834da42882add5e","intervals":[[1,52]],"path":"docs/promotion-policy.md"},{"blob":"2ac6ce40ff008f3269fdc03fe7bd0256cea418d5","intervals":[[1,2],[21,22],[53,53],[57,57],[61,63],[78,89],[165,165],[198,198],[222,222],[333,333],[353,354],[402,403],[424,424],[445,446],[450,450],[453,457],[476,476],[532,532],[609,609],[611,614],[616,618],[621,624],[626,626]],"path":"docs/w4-obligation-matrix.md"},{"blob":"e2e527ab7d765b9474911eab7eafbd2c0d10f259","intervals":[[2,2],[11,12],[15,29],[37,38],[47,47],[50,51],[61,68],[73,150],[154,154],[158,167],[176,185],[194,203],[208,233],[236,245],[250,250]],"path":"policy/templates/github-settings.json"}],"job_id":"8af537efc33d547bd72d8556ecac2bedad79bbe6dc473a4bf0abe243c647a205:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"entry":{"blob":"889e8e972ba2e6480412292d083138c9e7675